# Review

A system stays open to another change of a named kind when evidence can lead to an installed change that later operation depends on and the same revision functions remain available after the transition.

The title and opening paragraph put this claim within reach on a first reading. The six checks give it a concrete form, and the evidence section uses them to distinguish a change that took effect from evidence that the path survives the change.
